1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,963
OK, so we've been looking at the attitudes of various social

2
00:00:03,963 --> 00:00:07,380
and cultural groups towards the management of their personal finances

3
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,448
How important they feel it is to save money,

4
00:00:10,448 --> 00:00:12,970
and what they save their money for.

5
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:16,500
One aspect that we haven't yet considered is gender.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,513
So if we consider gender issues we're basically asking whether men

7
00:00:20,513 --> 00:00:23,620
and women have different attitudes towards saving money

8
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:26,350
and whether they save money for different things.

9
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:33,575
Back in 1928 the British writer George Bernard Shaw wrote in his Intelligent Women's Guide to Socialism

10
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:37,825
and Capitalism that 'A man is supposed to understand politics,

11
00:00:37,825 --> 00:00:42,500
economics and finance and is therefore unwilling to accept essential instruction.'

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:48,700
He also said, 'A woman, having fewer pretensions, is far more willing to learn'.

13
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:54,884
Now, though these days people might question a lot of the assumptions contained in those statements,

14
00:00:54,884 --> 00:00:59,908
recent research does suggest that there are some quite fundamental differences between men

15
00:00:59,908 --> 00:01:03,000
and women in their attitudes to economic matters.

16
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,060
Let's look at what men and women actually save for.

17
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:15,277
Research studies of women in North America have found that women are far more likely to save for their children's education

18
00:01:15,277 --> 00:01:21,120
and they are also more likely to save up in order to buy a house one day.

19
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:27,199
The same studies have found that men, on the other hand, tend to save for a car,

20
00:01:27,199 --> 00:01:32,920
which by the way takes a surprisingly large amount of the household budget in North America.

21
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:37,797
But the other main priority for men when saving money is their retirement.

22
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:44,550
When they're earning, they're far more likely to put money aside for their old age than women are.

23
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:46,606
Now this is rather disturbing,

24
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:54,420
because in fact the need for women to save for their old age is far greater than for men.

25
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:57,040
Let's consider this for a moment.

26
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:00,752
To start with, it is a fact that throughout the world,

27
00:02:00,752 --> 00:02:04,520
women are likely to live many years longer than men

28
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:07,500
so they need money to support them during this time.

29
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:12,415
Since women are likely to be the ones left without a partner in old age,

30
00:02:12,415 --> 00:02:16,320
they may therefore have to pay for nursing care

31
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,640
because they don't have a spouse to look after them.

32
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:25,460
Furthermore the high divorce rates in North America are creating a poverty cycle for women.

33
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:31,688
It is the divorced women who will most often have to look after the children

34
00:02:31,688 --> 00:02:37,500
and thus they need more money to look after not just themselves but others.

35
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:43,610
So what can be done about this situation?

36
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:49,440
The population in North America is likely to contain an increasing number of elderly women.

37
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:57,500
The research indicates that at present for women it takes a crisis to make them think about their future financial situation.

38
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:02,960
But of course this is the very worst time for anyone to make important decisions.

39
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:09,310
Women today need to look ahead, think ahead. Not wait until they're under pressure.

40
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:14,738
Even women in their early twenties need to think about pensions, for example, and

41
00:03:14,738 --> 00:03:21,330
with increasing numbers of women in professional positions there are signs that this is beginning to happen.

42
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:25,641
Then research also suggests that women avoid dealing effectively

43
00:03:25,641 --> 00:03:30,430
with their economic situation because of a lack of confidence.

44
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:36,042
The best way for them to overcome this is by getting themselves properly informed

45
00:03:36,042 --> 00:03:39,650
so they are less dependent on other people's advice.

46
00:03:39,650 --> 00:03:44,260
A number of initiatives have been set up to help them do this.

47
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:48,504
This College, for example, is one of the educational institutions

48
00:03:48,504 --> 00:03:51,760
which offers night classes in Money Management

49
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:55,720
and increasing numbers of women are enrolling on such courses.

50
00:03:55,720 --> 00:04:00,110
Here, they can be given advice on different ways of saving.

51
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:04,480
Many women are unwilling to invest in stocks and shares

52
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:07,890
for instance, but these can be extremely profitable.

53
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:15,599
It is usually advised that at least 70% of a person's savings should be in low-risk investments

54
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:21,040
but for the rest, financial advisors often advise taking some well-informed risks.

55
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:25,319
Initiatives such as this can give women the economic skills

56
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:29,170
and knowledge they need for a comfortable, independent retirement.

57
00:04:29,170 --> 00:04:36,100
The increasing proportion of elderly women in the population is likely to have other economic consequences...
